{"abstract":[{"text":"The Edmonds–Karp algorithm as a sequence of ","type":"text"},{"code":"EdmondsKarpEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s, pulled one at a time.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/flows\/edmondskarpevents"]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/EdmondsKarpEvents\/Iterator"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/EdmondsKarpEvents\/makeIterator()"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Type-Aliases","title":"Type Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/EdmondsKarpEvents\/Element"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/EdmondsKarpEvents\/Sequence-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdmondsKarpEvents"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AdditiveArithmetic","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edmonds–Karp, rather than Dinic, because each of its steps is one picture: a shortest path in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the residual network and the flow sent along it. Dinic’s blocking flows interleave advancing,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retreating and pruning within a level graph, which do not read as separate steps."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Making the sequence numbers the vertices and reads the capacities as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edmondsKarpMaximumFlow(from:to:capacity:)"},{"text":" does; each iterator builds its own residual","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"network and runs that call’s searches, in the same order, so the flows it sends are that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"call’s: the pushes less the cancellations on each edge are its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flow(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"text":", and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bottlenecks add up to its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"text":". The sequence holds no copy of the graph; its positions stay","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"valid until the graph is mutated. Stopping the loop stops the algorithm.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/EdmondsKarpEvents","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Flows\/ST"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:5F